{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# Bench Coil Characterisation — a real coil, outside any trap\n",
    "\n",
    "**Standalone.** This notebook shares no code with any other. Every driver, every capture\n",
    "routine and every fit is defined here, so it can be copied to a bare board and run on its\n",
    "own. ---\n",
    "\n",
    "## What this is for\n",
    "\n",
    "Every stage from 8 upward has measured a resonator whose answer was **chosen in software**.\n",
    "This one measures a physical coil sitting on the bench — no trap, no ion, no cryostat — where\n",
    "nothing is known in advance.\n",
    "\n",
    "That removes the project's central safeguard, so it is replaced by three others:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Replacement | What it catches |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **Self-test against the emulator, before and after** | Any fault in the instrument itself. The emulator is a register bit, not a cable, so it can be switched back in at any moment |\n",
    "| **Two independent measurements of the same width** | A fit that is wrong for a reason the fit cannot see — a sloping baseline, a stray tone, compression |\n",
    "| **A signal budget computed *and* measured** | Coupling, loading and level problems, which on a bench look exactly like physics |\n",
    "\n",
    "## The coil as wired\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook assumes the coil already has **0.3 pF coupling capacitors** on its drive and\n",
    "pickup ports. That is deliberately very weak coupling, and it has two consequences that shape\n",
    "everything below:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Good:** at 40 MHz a 0.3 pF capacitor is about 13 kΩ of reactance, so almost nothing is\n",
    "  drawn from the tank. The quality factor you measure should be close to the coil's own.\n",
    "- **Awkward:** the pickup capacitor and whatever capacitance follows it — cable, connector,\n",
    "  board input — form a capacitive divider, and 0.3 pF against even 20 pF of cable is a\n",
    "  division by seventy. **Keep the pickup lead as short as physically possible.** Step 3\n",
    "  measures what you actually got and says whether an amplifier is needed.\n",
    "\n",
    "## What this notebook cannot tell you\n",
    "\n",
    "Anything that needs an ion: the dip, resistive cooling, ion temperature, the phase-sensitive\n",
    "technique, the self-excited oscillator in its real form. Also anything needing electrodes,\n",
    "so nothing from Stage 17. None of that is on the critical path for proving the board works.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Before you run it\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Run Stage 12 first**, while the emulator is still the authority. It calibrates the two\n",
    "   decisions that only work on an emulator.\n",
    "2. Run this notebook **once with the input terminated** (set `COIL_CONNECTED = False`) to\n",
    "   catalogue the board's own stray signals, then again with the coil attached. Searching a\n",
    "   band you have not surveyed is how a stray signal becomes a discovery.\n",
    "3. As root: `sudo jupyter notebook` — everything here reads `/dev/mem`.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Order of the steps\n",
    "\n",
    "| Step | Question | Needs |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 0 | Is the right bitstream loaded and does everything answer? | — |\n",
    "| 1 | Does the instrument still return a known answer? | emulator |\n",
    "| 2 | Are the levels sane and what else is in the band? | coil or terminator |\n",
    "| 3 | Where is the resonance, and how sharp? | coil |\n",
    "| 4 | How much signal survives the 0.3 pF coupling? | coil |\n",
    "| 5 | Does a second, independent method agree? | coil |\n",
    "| 6 | Is the measurement linear — am I loading or compressing it? | coil |\n",
    "| 7 | Does anything move while I measure? | coil |\n",
    "| 8 | Does feedback change Q and centre as it should? | coil |\n",
    "| 9 | Summary, and the constants later notebooks need | — |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# Wiring the coil to the board\n",
    "\n",
    "**Two coaxial runs and one ground. That is the whole rig.** Read the current\n",
    "limit at the bottom before changing either capacitor - it is the only thing\n",
    "standing between a mistyped number and a damaged coil, and it is a piece of\n",
    "physics rather than a piece of software.\n",
    "\n",
    "## The picture\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "                 Red Pitaya STEMlab 125-14\n",
    "      +--------------------------------------------+\n",
    "      |                                            |\n",
    "      |   OUT1  (SMA)                   IN1  (SMA) |\n",
    "      +-----|--------------------------------|-----+\n",
    "            |                                |\n",
    "            |                                |\n",
    "      [ZFL-500LN+]                          |  short coax\n",
    "       28 dB, +15 V                         |\n",
    "            |  short coax                    |\n",
    "            |                                |\n",
    "         C_drive                          C_pick\n",
    "         0.3 pF                           0.3 pF\n",
    "            |                                |\n",
    "            |    +----------------------+    |\n",
    "            +----|   the coil / tank    |----+\n",
    "                 +----------------------+\n",
    "                            |\n",
    "                            |  ONE ground strap, at the board end only\n",
    "                            |\n",
    "                     board ground (SMA shells)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "| Board | Direction | Carries |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **OUT1** (DAC CH A) | out, to the coil | the drive **and** the feedback, already summed, via the **ZFL-500LN+** |\n",
    "| **IN1** (ADC CH A) | in, from the coil | everything this notebook measures |\n",
    "| **OUT2 / IN2** | - | unused. Leave them empty |\n",
    "| **E1 / E2 headers** | - | **never** for the coil. 3.3 V logic, no protection |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why only one output cable\n",
    "\n",
    "The feedback loop closes inside the chip: `dac_a_sum = asg_dat[0] + pid_dat[0]` sums the drive\n",
    "and the phase-shifted copy before the converter, saturating rather than wrapping. The emulator\n",
    "is a multiplexer in front of the phase shifter, so Step 1's self-test works with the coil still\n",
    "attached.\n",
    "\n",
    "## The two capacitors\n",
    "\n",
    "Series, one per port. They set the signal budget (0.3 pF against ~15 pF of cable and board is\n",
    "about −38 dB), block DC absolutely, and limit the current. Set the input jumper to **LV**\n",
    "(±1 V); the input is ~1 MΩ, so do not terminate it, and keep the coax short — every picofarad\n",
    "lands in `C_STRAY_EST`.\n",
    "\n",
    "## The current limit - the reason this is safe\n",
    "\n",
    "At the top of the search band the pickup capacitor's reactance is\n",
    "\n",
    "| frequency | reactance of 0.3 pF |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 20 MHz | 26.5 kΩ |\n",
    "| 41 MHz | 12.9 kΩ |\n",
    "| 55 MHz | 9.7 kΩ |\n",
    "\n",
    "OUT1 delivers at most ±1 V into 50 Ω, and `DRIVE_MAX = 0.9` caps it at 0.9 V.\n",
    "Through 12.9 kΩ that is **70 µA peak**, and the power it can deliver into *any*\n",
    "load - matched, mismatched, shorted, open - is bounded by\n",
    "\n",
    "    P_max = V² / (4 X_c) = 0.81 / (4 × 12850) ≈ **16 µW**\n",
    "\n",
    "Sixteen microwatts. There is no setting of `DRIVE_FRAC`, no feedback gain, and\n",
    "no software fault that gets past that, because the limit is the capacitor and\n",
    "not the code. The software guards in this notebook exist to protect the\n",
    "*measurement* - a clipped front end still looks vaguely like a resonance - not\n",
    "to protect the coil. The coil is protected by 0.3 pF of series reactance.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **The one change that removes this protection.** Replace either capacitor with\n",
    "> a direct connection, or with something in the nanofarad range, and OUT1 sees\n",
    "> 50 Ω instead of 13 kΩ: **18 mA and 8 mW**, about 500× more, and a fine-wire\n",
    "> coil can care about that. If you ever do that, recompute `DRIVE_MAX` from the\n",
    "> coil's own dissipation limit *before* the first run, and treat every number in\n",
    "> the configuration cell as untested.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## The amplifier\n",
    "\n",
    "A **Mini-Circuits ZFL-500LN+** sits in the **drive** path, between OUT1 and the drive capacitor.\n",
    "0.1–500 MHz, ~28 dB at 40 MHz, +5 dBm output rating, +15 V at 60 mA.\n",
    "\n",
    "It is in the drive path and not the pickup path for one reason: **the drive port is already fed\n",
    "from OUT1's 50 Ω source, so a 50 Ω amplifier costs nothing there.** The pickup port is\n",
    "high-impedance (1 MΩ ‖ ~15 pF ≈ 260 Ω at 40 MHz) and a 50 Ω input would throw away 14 dB before\n",
    "any gain arrived.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two limits, and they are not the same number:\n",
    "\n",
    "| | set by | value here |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **damage** | its *input* power, derated 20 dB for the open load | `DRIVE_MAX = 0.056` |\n",
    "| **compression** | its *output* power | working drive ≤ `0.0065` |\n",
    "\n",
    "`EXT_GAIN_DB` must be declared in the configuration cell. `DRIVE_MAX` is derived from it, Step 3\n",
    "ramps rather than jumping, and Step 4c refuses to continue if the measured gain exceeds what was\n",
    "declared — because that is the case where the ceiling is too permissive.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "**Everything you might want to change lives in this one cell.** Nothing below it is meant to\n",
    "be edited during normal use. Read the comments before the first run — three of these\n",
    "(`SEARCH_LO`, `SEARCH_HI`, `DRIVE_FRAC`) decide whether Step 4 finds anything at all."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# ============================ CONFIGURATION ==================================\n",
    "\n",
    "COIL_CONNECTED = True     # False = input terminated. Step 2 becomes a survey of the\n",
    "                          #   board's OWN stray signals, and Steps 3-8 are skipped.\n",
    "                          #   Run it that way ONCE before ever attaching the coil.\n",
    "\n",
    "SOURCE_NOTE    = 'bench coil, 0.3 pF coupling caps both ports, room temperature'\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- where to look for the resonance ---------------------------------------\n",
    "# Generous by default. Narrow it once you know roughly where the coil sits: the\n",
    "# coarse pass costs about one second per megahertz of span.\n",
    "SEARCH_LO      = 20.0e6   # [Hz] bottom of the search band\n",
    "SEARCH_HI      = 55.0e6   # [Hz] top. Must stay below 62.5 MHz (Nyquist)\n",
    "SEARCH_STEP    = 100e3    # [Hz] coarse grid. Must be FINER than the narrowest\n",
    "                          #   linewidth you could plausibly have, or the coarse\n",
    "                          #   pass steps straight over the resonance.\n",
    "                          #   Q = 1000 at 40 MHz is a 40 kHz linewidth -> use 20e3.\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- drive ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "DRIVE_FRAC     = 0.0032   # generator amplitude, 0..1 of full scale. Start high:\n",
    "                          #   0.3 pF throws most of it away. Step 6 checks that\n",
    "                          #   this is not so high that anything compresses.\n",
    "DRIVE_LIN_FRACS = [0.5, 0.71, 1.0]     # Step 6 ladder, as FRACTIONS of\n",
    "                          #   DRIVE_FRAC. Absolute values are a trap: once an\n",
    "                          #   amplifier is fitted DRIVE_FRAC drops by 40 dB and a\n",
    "                          #   fixed [0.225 ... 0.9] list would drive it far past\n",
    "                          #   its rating, or fail the DRIVE_MAX assert outright.\n",
    "                          #   Only 6 dB of span: with an amplifier fitted the\n",
    "                          #   working drive is already low, and a rung 12 dB\n",
    "                          #   below it sits in the receiver's noise floor, where\n",
    "                          #   the fitted \"peak\" is floor rather than signal.\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- the hard ceiling -------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "DRIVE_MAX      = 0.9      # THE ONLY NUMBER THAT LIMITS WHAT REACHES THE COIL.\n",
    "                          #   THE ONLY LIMIT ON WHAT REACHES THE COIL. Every\n",
    "                          #   amplitude write is checked against it and refused if\n",
    "                          #   larger. Must be in (0, 1.0].\n",
    "assert all(0.0 < x <= 1.0 for x in DRIVE_LIN_FRACS), \\\n",
    "    'DRIVE_LIN_FRACS are fractions of DRIVE_FRAC and must be in (0, 1]'\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- receiver ---------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "DEC_SEARCH     = 8        # log2(R) during the coarse search. R = 256, +-49 kHz\n",
    "                          #   clean band, 488 kHz output rate. Wide and quick.\n",
    "DEC_FIT        = 10       # log2(R) for the careful sweeps. R = 1024, +-12.2 kHz.\n",
    "                          #   Rule: the receiver window should be small next to\n",
    "                          #   the linewidth. Step 4 checks this and complains.\n",
    "N_AVG          = 64       # PEEK register pairs averaged per measurement point\n",
    "# ---- external amplifier in the DRIVE path (Step 4c) -------------------------\n",
    "G_PASSIVE      = 0.0158   # round-trip transfer measured with NO amplifier fitted.\n",
    "                          #   Step 4c infers the amplifier's output level from\n",
    "                          #   what arrives at the input, so this must be right.\n",
    "EXT_GAIN_DB     = 33.7    # [dB] gain of ANYTHING between OUT1 and the drive\n",
    "                          #   capacitor. 0.0 if nothing is fitted. Step 4c\n",
    "                          #   measures it and complains if this is wrong.\n",
    "#  TWO SEPARATE LIMITS, and conflating them is a mistake:\n",
    "#    DAMAGE is set by the amplifier's INPUT power  -> caps DRIVE_MAX\n",
    "#    COMPRESSION is set by its OUTPUT power        -> caps the working DRIVE_FRAC\n",
    "#  They differ by the gain, so for a ZFL-500LN+ they are 0.056 and 0.0065 - a\n",
    "#  factor of nine. Steps that only need the drive to EXIST (the Step 1 self-test,\n",
    "#  where the emulator replaces the input and the amplifier is irrelevant) may use\n",
    "#  the damage limit. Steps that measure the coil must stay under the other.\n",
    "EXT_PAD_DB      = 0.0     # [dB] fixed attenuation between OUT1 and the\n",
    "                          #   amplifier. It decides whether SELF-OSCILLATION can\n",
    "                          #   be explored at all: an oscillating loop puts FULL\n",
    "                          #   SCALE (+10 dBm) into the DAC, and gen.amp()'s\n",
    "                          #   ceiling does not apply to the feedback path. The\n",
    "                          #   amplifier then sees 10 - EXT_PAD_DB dBm, which must\n",
    "                          #   stay under AMP_IN_MAX_DBM.\n",
    "AMP_IN_MAX_DBM  = -15.0   # [dBm] max input for NO DAMAGE. +5 dBm normally, but\n",
    "                          #   both datasheets derate by 20 dB with no load, and a\n",
    "                          #   0.3 pF capacitor IS an open load at 40 MHz. Use +5\n",
    "                          #   if you fit a 50 ohm terminator at the output.\n",
    "AMP_OUT_MAX_DBM = 0.0     # [dBm] linear output ceiling. 0 dBm for a ZFL-500LN+\n",
    "                          #   into an open load: its +7.9 dBm compression figure\n",
    "                          #   is into 50 ohm and an open load doubles the voltage.\n",
    "AMP_TEST_START = 0.001    # first drive of the ladder. Safe for any gain up to\n",
    "                          #   40 dB: OUT1 is -44 dBm here, so even 40 dB of gain\n",
    "                          #   lands at -4 dBm, well inside the rating.\n",
    "AMP_TEST_STEP  = 1.6      # multiplier per rung, about 4 dB\n",
    "\n",
    "GUARD_NSAMP    = 256      # scope samples per input-level check. The guard runs at\n",
    "                          #   samples per input-level check. Runs at every swept\n",
    "                          #   point, so it dominates a sweep's time.\n",
    "SETTLE         = 0.02     # [s] wait after any retune, for the filter pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Step 3: signal budget ---------------------------------------------------\n",
    "C_COUPLE       = 0.3e-12  # [F] the coupling capacitors actually fitted\n",
    "# ---- after the pickup capacitor ---------------------------------------------\n",
    "#  A transfer measurement determines (C_COUPLE + C_stray) and nothing else, so\n",
    "#  the split below rests on C_COUPLE being its marked value and scales with it:\n",
    "#  0.2 pF would make C_BOARD_IN 7.7 pF, 0.4 pF would make it 15.3 pF. Step 4b\n",
    "#  prints the measurement that would settle it.\n",
    "C_BOARD_IN     = 11.5e-12 # [F] the board's own input capacitance. Derived, not\n",
    "                          #   measured - see above.\n",
    "C_CABLE_PICKUP = 13.0e-12 # [F] the pickup cable. From the two-length experiment:\n",
    "                          #   doubling it moved the transfer by -3.7 dB, which\n",
    "                          #   requires 13.0 pF per length. ~13 cm at 100 pF/m.\n",
    "C_STRAY_EST    = C_BOARD_IN + C_CABLE_PICKUP\n",
    "                          # [F] the sum is what the transfer constrains.\n",
    "L_COIL         = 423.5e-9   # [H] coil inductance\n",
    "L_COIL_ERR     = 11.8e-9    # [H] its uncertainty\n",
    "C_COIL         = 1.59e-12   # [F] the coil's own self-capacitance\n",
    "C_COIL_ERR     = 0.06e-12   # [F] its uncertainty\n",
    "\n",
    "C_PARALLEL     = 39.0e-12   # [F] the capacitor fitted ACROSS the tank to emulate\n",
    "                            #   the trap's parasitic capacitance. Without it the\n",
    "                            #   coil sits near 165 MHz, above Nyquist, and is\n",
    "                            #   invisible to this board.\n",
    "C_PARALLEL_ERR = 2.0e-12    # [F] the capacitor's tolerance. A 5% part on 39 pF is\n",
    "                            #   +-1.95 pF, and it DOMINATES the predicted centre\n",
    "                            #   frequency - it is 25x the coil's own capacitance.\n",
    "                            #   If you know the part is 1% or 2%, put that in:\n",
    "                            #   Step 4b's agreement test is only as tight as this.\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- an independent instrument, if you have one -----------------------------\n",
    "#  A vector network analyser measuring the same resonator is the strongest\n",
    "#  cross-check available: different source, different detector, different\n",
    "#  analysis. Set these and Step 4b compares against them. None to skip.\n",
    "VNA_F0         = 39.976e6   # [Hz] centre from the VNA, or None\n",
    "VNA_Q          = 181.0      # quality factor from the VNA, or None\n",
    "\n",
    "L_EST          = L_COIL   # [H] used by Step 4's thermal-noise estimate. Set to\n",
    "                          #   None to skip that block rather than guess.\n",
    "R_IN_BOARD     = 1.0e6    # [ohm] the board's input resistance\n",
    "V_FULLSCALE    = 1.0      # [V] input full scale. 1.0 on the LV jumper setting,\n",
    "                          #   20.0 on HV. Used only to print volts instead of\n",
    "                          #   counts - nothing depends on it being right.\n",
    "T_COIL         = 293.0    # [K] coil temperature, for the thermal-noise estimate\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Step 7: drift -----------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "DRIFT_MINUTES  = 10.0     # total observation time\n",
    "DRIFT_PERIOD   = 20.0     # [s] between revisits\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Step 8: feedback --------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "FB_PHASES      = list(range(0, 360, 20))   # [deg] phase axis. Must stay\n",
    "                          #   symmetric - every phase needs its opposite present,\n",
    "                          #   because Step 8 subtracts the two.\n",
    "FB_GAIN_MAX    = 1.90     # ceiling on the feedback coefficient. The register is\n",
    "                          #   Q2.14 and A x 16384 must fit in int16: at A = 2.0\n",
    "                          #   the coefficient wraps to -32768 and the feedback\n",
    "                          #   SILENTLY INVERTS. PhaseShift.set() refuses anything\n",
    "                          #   from 1.99 up; this stays clear of it.\n",
    "FB_GAIN_PROBE  = 1.50     # gain used to FIND the two special phases.\n",
    "                          #   High on purpose: through two 0.3 pF capacitors the\n",
    "                          #   round trip loses ~34 dB, so K reaches only a few\n",
    "                          #   percent even at the register ceiling. The input\n",
    "                          #   level guard is unchanged and still checked.\n",
    "FB_GAIN_FRACS  = [0.15, 0.3, 0.45, 0.6, 0.75, 0.9, 1.0]\n",
    "                          # gains for Step 8b as FRACTIONS of the usable ceiling.\n",
    "                          #   Absolute values get filtered out entirely whenever\n",
    "                          #   the coupling improves and the ceiling drops.\n",
    "FB_NAVG        = 96       # averages per point in Step 8. Higher than anywhere\n",
    "                          #   else: the signature being looked for is a few\n",
    "                          #   percent of Q, so the fit noise has to go below it.\n",
    "# ---- Step 8c: the gain/phase map ------------------------------------------\n",
    "FB_MAP_PHASES  = 24       # phase steps across 360 degrees\n",
    "FB_MAP_GAINS   = 12       # gain steps from zero to the usable ceiling\n",
    "FB_MAP_NPTS    = 15       # frequency points per pixel. The line NARROWS as the\n",
    "                          #   gain rises, so the grid tracks the previous pixel's\n",
    "                          #   fit rather than staying fixed - a span set for the\n",
    "                          #   unfed line puts only one point across a line that\n",
    "                          #   feedback has narrowed five-fold.\n",
    "FB_MAP_NAVG    = 32       # averages per point. Lower than the 1D sweep: on the\n",
    "                          #   map the effect is tens of percent, not one percent.\n",
    "FB_MAP_SETTLE  = 0.010    # [s] per point\n",
    "FB_OSC_LEVEL   = 0.10     # input fraction, DRIVE OFF, above which the loop is\n",
    "                          #   judged to be self-oscillating.\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Step 8d: the lineshape family, positive and negative feedback ---------\n",
    "FB_SPEC_FRACS  = [-0.95, -0.70, -0.40, 0.0, 0.40, 0.70, 0.90, 0.95]\n",
    "                          # fractions of the usable ceiling. NEGATIVE means the\n",
    "                          #   opposite phase - the coefficient register cannot go\n",
    "                          #   negative, but phi + 180 is the same thing.\n",
    "# ---- Step 8e: how far and how accurately the resonance can be moved --------\n",
    "FB_SHIFT_FRACS = [0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8, 0.95]\n",
    "FB_SHIFT_TESTS = 3        # target shifts to request and then verify     # input fraction, DRIVE OFF, above which the loop is\n",
    "                          #   judged to be self-oscillating. Those pixels are\n",
    "                          #   left blank and drawn black, as in the paper.\n",
    "\n",
    "FB_LEVEL_GUARD = 0.80     # abort the point if the input exceeds this fraction of\n",
    "                          #   full scale. THE REAL PATH HAS NO OVERLOAD FLAG - the\n",
    "                          #   emulator's sticky CLIPPED bit has quietly been doing\n",
    "                          #   that job for ten stages and it is gone here.\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Step 1: instrument self-test -------------------------------------------\n",
    "SELFTEST_F0    = 37.0e6   # deliberately NOT 40 MHz, so a hard-coded 40 MHz\n",
    "SELFTEST_Q     = 250.0    #   anywhere in the analysis would show up as a failure\n",
    "SELFTEST_TOL_F = 0.20     # tolerance: fraction of a linewidth on the centre\n",
    "SELFTEST_TOL_Q = 0.05     # tolerance: fractional error on Q\n",
    "\n",
    "RESULTS_JSON   = 'bench_coil_results.json'   # written by Step 9\n",
    "\n",
    "FS_CLK         = 125e6    # the one clock everything on the board runs from [Hz]\n",
    "# ---- checks that need definitions from further down ------------------------\n",
    "# External gain sits outside anything the software can see, so fold it into the\n",
    "# ceiling here. With an amplifier fitted, DRIVE_MAX is set by what the AMPLIFIER\n",
    "# can deliver, not by what the converter can.\n",
    "if EXT_GAIN_DB > 0.0:\n",
    "    # A pad in front of the amplifier raises BOTH limits by its value, and it is\n",
    "    # the only way to give the converter a decent number of counts to work with:\n",
    "    # the amplifier's output ceiling caps the delivered power either way, so\n",
    "    # without a pad the DAC ends up running at a couple of dozen counts.\n",
    "    DRIVE_MAX = min(DRIVE_MAX,\n",
    "                    10.0 ** ((AMP_IN_MAX_DBM + EXT_PAD_DB - 10.0) / 20.0))\n",
    "    DRIVE_LINEAR_MAX = 10.0 ** ((AMP_OUT_MAX_DBM - EXT_GAIN_DB + EXT_PAD_DB\n",
    "                                 - 10.0) / 20.0)\n",
    "    print('external gain %.1f dB: DRIVE_MAX %.4f (damage), linear limit %.4f'\n",
    "          % (EXT_GAIN_DB, DRIVE_MAX, DRIVE_LINEAR_MAX))\n",
    "    if DRIVE_FRAC > DRIVE_LINEAR_MAX:\n",
    "        print('  WARNING: DRIVE_FRAC %.4f is above the linear limit - the'\n",
    "              % DRIVE_FRAC)\n",
    "        print('  amplifier will compress and the feedback measurements will be')\n",
    "        print('  wrong. Safe, but not useful. Use about %.4f.'\n",
    "              % (0.5 * DRIVE_LINEAR_MAX))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    DRIVE_LINEAR_MAX = DRIVE_MAX\n",
    "\n",
    "# The Step 1 self-test drives the EMULATOR, which replaces the digitised input,\n",
    "# so the amplifier plays no part in what it measures - only the damage limit\n",
    "# applies. It needs a large signal to hit its 5% tolerance on Q.\n",
    "SELFTEST_DRIVE = min(0.3, 0.9 * DRIVE_MAX)\n",
    "\n",
    "assert 0.0 < DRIVE_MAX <= 1.0, 'DRIVE_MAX must be in (0, 1.0]'\n",
    "assert 0.0 <= DRIVE_FRAC <= DRIVE_MAX, (\n",
    "    'DRIVE_FRAC %.4f exceeds DRIVE_MAX %.4f. With %.1f dB of external gain the '\n",
    "    'amplifier would be driven far past its rating. Use about %.4f.'\n",
    "    % (DRIVE_FRAC, DRIVE_MAX, EXT_GAIN_DB, 0.5 * DRIVE_MAX))\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- feedback checks, down here because they need the Step 8 block above ----\n",
    "assert 0.0 < FB_GAIN_MAX < 1.99, 'FB_GAIN_MAX must be below the 1.99 register limit'\n",
    "assert 0.0 <= FB_GAIN_PROBE <= FB_GAIN_MAX, 'FB_GAIN_PROBE exceeds FB_GAIN_MAX'\n",
    "assert all(0.0 < fr <= 1.0 for fr in FB_GAIN_FRACS), \\\n",
    "    'FB_GAIN_FRACS are fractions of the usable ceiling and must be in (0, 1]'\n",
    "assert len(FB_PHASES) % 2 == 0 and all(((p + 180) % 360) in FB_PHASES for p in FB_PHASES), \\\n",
    "    'FB_PHASES must contain the opposite of every phase it contains'\n",
    "\n",
    "print('configuration loaded. coil connected: %s' % COIL_CONNECTED)\n",
    "print('search band %.1f - %.1f MHz in %.0f kHz steps'\n",
    "      % (SEARCH_LO / 1e6, SEARCH_HI / 1e6, SEARCH_STEP / 1e3))"
   ]
