    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 0 — Is the right thing loaded, and does everything answer?\n",
    "\n",
    "Four questions, all cheap, all worth asking before anything else. The first is the one that\n",
    "has cost this project the most time: **loading an old bitstream looks exactly like success.**\n",
    "The light blinks, registers answer, and measurements look plausible. The build identifier at\n",
    "register `0x48` is a hash of the Verilog the bitstream was built from — if it reads zero, the\n",
    "bitstream was not produced by `build_project.tcl` and may contain stale logic.\n",
    "\n",
    "The emulator probe matters for a subtler reason: an older bitstream has a *stub* at that\n",
    "address which answers every read with zero and looks politely dead. Step 1 would then compare\n",
    "against nothing at all and pass."
   ]
  },
