    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 1 — Does the instrument still return a known answer?\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the replacement for everything the emulator used to provide, and it is worth\n",
    "understanding why it still works with a coil bolted to the input.\n",
    "\n",
    "The emulator does not sit *beside* the input path — enabled, it **replaces the digitised\n",
    "input entirely**. So the coil can stay connected, cabled and irrelevant. That means the\n",
    "known-answer check is not a one-way door you walk through once: it is available at any moment,\n",
    "including between two real measurements that disagree.\n",
    "\n",
    "The test sets a centre and a quality factor the analysis is never told, sweeps, fits, and\n",
    "demands the fit return them. The comparison is against the **quantised** values — the\n",
    "coefficients are 18-bit integers, so the emulator's true centre and Q are those recovered from\n",
    "the rounded coefficients, not the numbers requested. Comparing against the requested numbers\n",
    "would build a small permanent error into the tolerance.\n",
    "\n",
    "`SELFTEST_F0` is deliberately not 40 MHz. If any part of the analysis had a 40 MHz constant\n",
    "baked into it, this would fail rather than quietly agree.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run this cell again at the end of the session.** If it passes both times, nothing about the\n",
    "instrument changed while you were measuring the coil."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 1 - INSTRUMENT SELF-TEST AGAINST A KNOWN ANSWER\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "def instrument_selftest(verbose=True):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Switch the emulator in, measure it, and demand the answer it was given.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns a dict. Leaves the emulator DISABLED whatever happens.\"\"\"\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        f0_q, q_q = emu.config(SELFTEST_F0, SELFTEST_Q, delay=15, oshift=7)\n",
    "        lw_q = f0_q / q_q\n",
    "        emu.clear()\n",
    "        emu.enable()\n",
    "\n",
    "        acq.start(DEC_FIT)\n",
    "        ps.off()\n",
    "\n",
    "        # +-2.5 linewidths is the whole curve, not just its top. SELFTEST_DRIVE\n",
    "        # is capped at 0.3 to keep the emulator's 25-bit state clear of\n",
    "        # saturation, and at the amplifier's damage limit when one is fitted.\n",
    "        grid = f0_q + np.linspace(-2.5, 2.5, 25) * lw_q\n",
    "        f, z = sweep(grid, drive_frac=SELFTEST_DRIVE)\n",
    "        gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "        if emu.clipped():\n",
    "            raise RuntimeError('the emulator saturated - lower the self-test drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "        fit = fit_lorentzian(f, np.abs(z) ** 2)\n",
    "        err_f = (fit['f0'] - f0_q) / lw_q            # in linewidths\n",
    "        err_q = fit['Q'] / q_q - 1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "        ok = (abs(err_f) <= SELFTEST_TOL_F) and (abs(err_q) <= SELFTEST_TOL_Q)\n",
    "        if verbose:\n",
    "            print('known answer (quantised) : f0 = %.6f MHz, Q = %.1f, lw = %.1f kHz'\n",
    "                  % (f0_q / 1e6, q_q, lw_q / 1e3))\n",
    "            print('measured                 : f0 = %.6f MHz, Q = %.1f'\n",
    "                  % (fit['f0'] / 1e6, fit['Q']))\n",
    "            print('error                    : centre %+.3f linewidths, Q %+.2f%%'\n",
    "                  % (err_f, 100 * err_q))\n",
    "            print('fit residual             : %.4f of peak' % fit['resid'])\n",
    "            print('-' * 68)\n",
    "            print('%s - the instrument %s reproduce an answer it was given'\n",
    "                  % ('PASS' if ok else 'FAIL', 'can' if ok else 'CANNOT'))\n",
    "        return dict(ok=ok, f0_known=f0_q, q_known=q_q, f0_meas=fit['f0'],\n",
    "                    q_meas=fit['Q'], err_f_lw=err_f, err_q_frac=err_q,\n",
    "                    resid=fit['resid'], f=f, z=z, fit=fit)\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        emu.disable()\n",
    "        gen.off()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 1 - instrument self-test (emulator in, coil ignored)')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "st1_before = instrument_selftest()\n",
    "print('emulator disabled - the board is listening to its real input again')"
   ]
  },
