   "source": [
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 3 — Find the resonance without being told where it is\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything from Stage 8 upward has been *handed* the answer, and about forty places downstream\n",
    "read it back. Here there is nothing to hand over. Three widening passes:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Pass | What it does | Why that way |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Look around** | Step across the whole plausible band, few averages, no fitting | It only has to find the neighbourhood. Nothing is fitted, so there is nothing to be fooled by |\n",
    "| **Bracket** | Widen around the best candidate until the curve clearly comes back down on *both* sides | A fit interpolating between points is trustworthy; one extrapolating past them is not |\n",
    "| **Refine** | A dense sweep at a decimation chosen from the width just estimated, then fit | The receiver window must be small next to the linewidth or the window smears the curve |\n",
    "\n",
    "**`SEARCH_STEP` is the parameter that decides whether this works.** The coarse pass cannot find\n",
    "a line narrower than its own step — it walks straight over it. If nothing is found, halve the\n",
    "step before doing anything else.\n",
    "\n",
    "The receiver is retuned to each drive frequency, so the response is always read at zero\n",
    "frequency. That is why the coarse pass can be quick and still be exact."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 3 - FIND THE RESONANCE\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "def choose_dec(lw):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Pick log2(decimation) so the receiver window is small next to a linewidth.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Aim: clean half-window <= lw/10, i.e. 0.1 x output_rate <= lw/10, i.e.\n",
    "    output_rate <= lw. Clamped to 8..12, because below R = 256 the droop\n",
    "    corrector bypasses itself and above R = 4096 the hardware stops.\"\"\"\n",
    "    d = int(np.ceil(np.log2(FS_CLK / max(lw, 1.0))))\n",
    "    return int(min(12, max(8, d)))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def half_power_width(f, p):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Crude width straight off the data: the span above half the peak.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Deliberately not a fit. Used only to decide how wide the next sweep should\n",
    "    be, where being fooled by a fit would be worse than being approximate.\"\"\"\n",
    "    p = np.asarray(p, dtype=float)\n",
    "    base = float(np.median(p))\n",
    "    half = base + 0.5 * (float(np.max(p)) - base)\n",
    "    above = np.where(p >= half)[0]\n",
    "    if len(above) < 2:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    return float(f[above[-1]] - f[above[0]])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "if not COIL_CONNECTED:\n",
    "    raise SystemExit('COIL_CONNECTED is False - Steps 3 onwards need the coil. '\n",
    "                     'Stop here; the survey above is the deliverable for this run.')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 3 - find the resonance')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "\n",
    "emu.disable()\n",
    "ps.off()\n",
    "preflight_drive(0.5 * (SEARCH_LO + SEARCH_HI))\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- pass 1: look around -----------------------------------------------------\n",
    "acq.start(DEC_SEARCH)\n",
    "grid1 = np.arange(SEARCH_LO, SEARCH_HI + SEARCH_STEP, SEARCH_STEP)\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "f1, z1 = sweep(grid1, drive_frac=DRIVE_FRAC, navg=16, settle=0.006,\n",
    "               level_guard=0.95)\n",
    "gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "p1 = np.abs(z1) ** 2\n",
    "k1 = int(np.argmax(p1))\n",
    "contrast_db = 10 * np.log10(p1[k1] / max(np.median(p1), 1e-300))\n",
    "print('pass 1: %d points in %.0f s' % (len(grid1), time.time() - t0))\n",
    "print('        best candidate %.4f MHz, %.1f dB above the median'\n",
    "      % (f1[k1] / 1e6, contrast_db))\n",
    "_pk_counts = float(np.sqrt(p1[k1]))\n",
    "print('        peak response %.0f counts' % _pk_counts)\n",
    "if _pk_counts < 20.0:\n",
    "    print('        WARNING: under 20 counts. Whatever is fitted below will be')\n",
    "    print('        noise. Check the drive, the coupling, and whether an external')\n",
    "    print('        amplifier is declared in EXT_GAIN_DB but not actually fitted.')\n",
    "if contrast_db < 6.0:\n",
    "    print('        WARNING: less than 6 dB of contrast. Either the coil is not')\n",
    "    print('        coupled, the drive is too small, or SEARCH_STEP is stepping')\n",
    "    print('        over a narrow line. Halve SEARCH_STEP and try again.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# --- pass 2: bracket ---------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "#  Widen until the curve comes down on BOTH sides. Each attempt doubles the\n",
    "#  span. Stopping as soon as both flanks are below half the peak is what makes\n",
    "#  the later fit an interpolation rather than an extrapolation.\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "span = 6.0 * SEARCH_STEP\n",
    "f_c = f1[k1]\n",
    "lw_guess = None\n",
    "for attempt in range(5):\n",
    "    grid2 = f_c + np.linspace(-span, span, 41)\n",
    "    grid2 = grid2[(grid2 > 1.0e6) & (grid2 < 0.49 * FS_CLK)]\n",
    "    f2, z2 = sweep(grid2, drive_frac=DRIVE_FRAC, navg=24, settle=0.008,\n",
    "                   level_guard=0.95)\n",
    "    gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "    p2 = np.abs(z2) ** 2\n",
    "    base2 = float(np.median(p2))\n",
    "    half = base2 + 0.5 * (float(np.max(p2)) - base2)\n",
    "    down_both = (p2[0] < half) and (p2[-1] < half)\n",
    "    f_c = float(f2[int(np.argmax(p2))])\n",
    "    lw_guess = half_power_width(f2, p2)\n",
    "    print('pass 2 attempt %d: span +-%.1f kHz, centre %.4f MHz, '\n",
    "          'flanks down both sides: %s'\n",
    "          % (attempt + 1, span / 1e3, f_c / 1e6, down_both))\n",
    "    if down_both and lw_guess:\n",
    "        break\n",
    "    span *= 2.0\n",
    "\n",
    "if lw_guess is None:\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError('could not bracket a resonance - widen SEARCH or check coupling')\n",
    "print('        rough linewidth %.1f kHz  ->  rough Q %.0f'\n",
    "      % (lw_guess / 1e3, f_c / lw_guess))"
