   "source": [
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 7 — Does anything move while you are measuring?\n",
    "\n",
    "The emulated coil was exactly constant for as long as you cared to look. A real one is not: it\n",
    "answers to room temperature, to airflow, and to anything mechanical. A full feedback map takes\n",
    "several minutes, and if the centre moves during the scan the map smears in a way that looks\n",
    "like real structure.\n",
    "\n",
    "This revisits the same measurement at intervals and reports two different things, which are\n",
    "easy to conflate and matter for different reasons:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Drift** — a slow, one-way trend. It biases a long scan. Measured as the straight-line\n",
    "  slope over the whole run.\n",
    "- **Scatter** — point-to-point wobble. It sets the floor on any single measurement. Measured\n",
    "  as the deviation about that line.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both are reported *in linewidths*, because that is the unit in which they either matter or do\n",
    "not. A drift of a hundredth of a linewidth over ten minutes is irrelevant; a tenth is not."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 7 - DRIFT AND SCATTER\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 7 - drift over %.0f minutes, sampled every %.0f s'\n",
    "      % (DRIFT_MINUTES, DRIFT_PERIOD))\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "\n",
    "acq.start(DEC_USE)\n",
    "grid7 = F0 + np.linspace(-2.0, 2.0, 21) * LW      # short: this runs many times\n",
    "\n",
    "t_start = time.time()\n",
    "d_t, d_f0, d_q = [], [], []\n",
    "\n",
    "while time.time() - t_start < DRIFT_MINUTES * 60.0:\n",
    "    t_point = time.time()\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        f7, z7 = sweep(grid7, drive_frac=DRIVE_FRAC, navg=32, level_guard=0.95)\n",
    "        gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "        fit7 = fit_lorentzian(f7, np.abs(z7) ** 2)\n",
    "        d_t.append(t_point - t_start)\n",
    "        d_f0.append(fit7['f0'])\n",
    "        d_q.append(fit7['Q'])\n",
    "        print('  %6.1f s : f0 %+9.1f Hz from start, Q = %6.1f'\n",
    "              % (d_t[-1], d_f0[-1] - d_f0[0], d_q[-1]))\n",
    "    except Exception as exc:\n",
    "        # One bad fit must not end a twenty-minute run. Record and continue.\n",
    "        print('  %6.1f s : fit failed (%s)' % (time.time() - t_start, exc))\n",
    "    time.sleep(max(0.0, DRIFT_PERIOD - (time.time() - t_point)))\n",
    "\n",
    "gen.off()\n",
    "d_t = np.array(d_t); d_f0 = np.array(d_f0); d_q = np.array(d_q)\n",
    "\n",
    "if len(d_t) < 4:\n",
    "    # Do not leave the summary printing nan. If the fits failed this often the\n",
    "    # cause is upstream and saying so is more use than a blank.\n",
    "    DRIFT_HZ_PER_MIN = SCATTER_HZ = float('nan')\n",
    "    print('ONLY %d USABLE POINTS OUT OF %d ATTEMPTS - drift not characterised.'\n",
    "          % (len(d_t), max(1, int(DRIFT_MINUTES * 60.0 / max(DRIFT_PERIOD, 1e-9)))))\n",
    "    print('The fits themselves are failing, not the coil. Check the Step 3')\n",
    "    print('residual and the leak figure before re-running this step.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    slope, icept = np.polyfit(d_t, d_f0, 1)\n",
    "    resid = d_f0 - (slope * d_t + icept)\n",
    "    DRIFT_HZ_PER_MIN = slope * 60.0\n",
    "    SCATTER_HZ = float(np.std(resid))\n",
    "    total = slope * d_t[-1]\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  drift    : %+.1f Hz/min  =  %+.4f linewidths/min'\n",
    "          % (DRIFT_HZ_PER_MIN, DRIFT_HZ_PER_MIN / LW))\n",
    "    print('  over the whole run: %+.0f Hz = %+.3f linewidths' % (total, total / LW))\n",
    "    print('  scatter  : %.1f Hz  =  %.4f linewidths' % (SCATTER_HZ, SCATTER_HZ / LW))\n",
    "    print('  Q scatter: %.1f%%' % (100 * np.std(d_q) / np.mean(d_q)))\n",
    "    print('-' * 68)\n",
    "    # A feedback map takes minutes; if the centre moves an appreciable fraction\n",
    "    # of a linewidth in that time the map is of several different systems.\n",
    "    map_minutes = 7.0\n",
    "    move = abs(DRIFT_HZ_PER_MIN) * map_minutes / LW\n",
    "    print('  a %.0f-minute scan would see the centre move %.3f linewidths'\n",
    "          % (map_minutes, move))\n",
    "    if move > 0.10:\n",
    "        print('  -> that is enough to smear a map. Either shorten the scan, or')\n",
    "        print('     run a servo during it (Stage 9 Step 4 has one), or re-centre')\n",
    "        print('     between rows.')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('  -> negligible. A scan can run open-loop.')\n",
    "\n",
    "    fig, (b1, b2) = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(7.5, 4.6), sharex=True)\n",
    "    b1.plot(d_t / 60.0, (d_f0 - d_f0[0]) / 1e3, 'o-', ms=3.5, lw=1.0)\n",
    "    b1.plot(d_t / 60.0, (slope * d_t + icept - d_f0[0]) / 1e3, '-', lw=1.2,\n",
    "            color=CLR_ORANGE, label='linear drift')\n",
    "    b1.set_ylabel('centre shift / kHz')\n",
    "    b1.legend(fontsize=8)\n",
    "    b1.set_title('Step 7 - drift %+.1f Hz/min, scatter %.1f Hz'\n",
    "                 % (DRIFT_HZ_PER_MIN, SCATTER_HZ))\n",
    "    b2.plot(d_t / 60.0, d_q, 'o-', ms=3.5, lw=1.0, color=CLR_GREEN)\n",
    "    b2.set_xlabel('time / minutes')\n",
    "    b2.set_ylabel('Q')\n",
    "    plt.show()"
   ]
