   "source": [
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 8 — Feedback against a real coil\n",
    "\n",
    "The flagship measurement, on hardware that is no longer pretending. Feedback takes the coil's\n",
    "own signal, shifts its phase, scales it and adds it back, which changes two things about the\n",
    "resonator: the **quality factor** (feedback aligned with the coil's motion cancels part of its\n",
    "loss) and the **centre frequency** (feedback aligned with the coil's displacement acts like\n",
    "changing the tuning).\n",
    "\n",
    "Three things are different from every previous stage, and all three are handled by measuring\n",
    "rather than assuming:\n",
    "\n",
    "**1. The phase axis is not meaningful in absolute terms.** The loop now runs through cables,\n",
    "connectors and the coil itself, adding delay the phase shifter's latency correction cannot\n",
    "know about. So the two special phases are *found*, and everything is reported relative to\n",
    "them. A fixed offset in the phase axis is expected and is not an error.\n",
    "\n",
    "**2. There is no overload flag.** The emulator's sticky clip bit has quietly been the guard\n",
    "for ten stages and it is gone. Every point below checks the raw input level first and abandons\n",
    "the point rather than fitting nonsense.\n",
    "\n",
    "**3. The loop may simply not have enough gain, and that is a result.** The feedback crosses\n",
    "both coupling capacitors — out through one, back through the other — so it carries the ~1/100\n",
    "divider *twice*. Step 4 measures the one-way transfer and Step 8 turns it into a budget before\n",
    "it sweeps anything: `K = A × G_fwd`, with `A` capped at 1.9 by the coefficient register. If\n",
    "that product cannot reach a percent or so, no phase is going to look different from any other,\n",
    "and the notebook says so up front rather than letting an `argmax` invent a narrowing phase out\n",
    "of fit noise. **This is the measurement the notebook's name is about.** An amplifier in the\n",
    "pickup path is what changes the answer, and this is the number that justifies fitting one.\n",
    "\n",
    "**4. Everything is measured differentially.** Feedback is antisymmetric in phase — what narrows\n",
    "the line at φ broadens it at φ+180 — while drift, baseline bias and a sagging drive are not.\n",
    "Subtracting the opposite phase cancels those and doubles the signal, and the result is compared\n",
    "against the measurement's own point-to-point scatter before any phase is named.\n",
    "\n",
    "**5. Self-oscillation is approached, not entered.** Past a certain gain the loop's net loss\n",
    "goes negative and the coil sustains itself. On the emulator that was safe and bisecting to the\n",
    "boundary was a measurement. Here the loop saturates the input instead, and a saturated input\n",
    "produces a distorted shape that still looks vaguely like a resonance — this project's\n",
    "signature failure. So the boundary is **extrapolated** from the linear region and deliberately\n",
    "not walked into. Entering it should be a separate, deliberate experiment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 8a - THE PHASE AXIS: find the two special phases\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 8 - feedback on the real coil')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "\n",
    "acq.start(DEC_USE)\n",
    "whole, frac = ps.config_delay(F0)\n",
    "print('quarter-period delay line: %d whole clocks + %.3f' % (whole, frac))\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  LOOP-GAIN BUDGET\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  The feedback path crosses BOTH coupling capacitors, so the round trip carries\n",
    "#  the divider twice. Step 4 measured the one-way half as G_FWD, so K = A x G_FWD\n",
    "#  and K = 1 is self-oscillation.\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "_HEADROOM = 0.95 - DRIVE_FRAC\n",
    "if _HEADROOM <= 0.0:\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError('DRIVE_FRAC = %.2f leaves no converter headroom for any '\n",
    "                       'feedback at all. Lower it before running Step 8.'\n",
    "                       % DRIVE_FRAC)\n",
    "#  CLOSED-LOOP. Feedback multiplies the converter signal by 1/(1-K), so dividing\n",
    "#  the headroom by the OPEN-loop level under-estimates it badly once K is large.\n",
    "#     DAC:  A <= (H-D) / (D*r + G*(H-D))       ADC:  A <= (1 - D*r/guard) / G\n",
    "_r = raw_peak / max(DRIVE_FRAC, 1e-9)          # peak-based transfer\n",
    "_H = 0.95\n",
    "_a_dac = (_H - DRIVE_FRAC) / max(DRIVE_FRAC * _r + G_FWD_RES * (_H - DRIVE_FRAC), 1e-12)\n",
    "_a_adc = (1.0 - DRIVE_FRAC * _r / FB_LEVEL_GUARD) / max(G_FWD_RES, 1e-12)\n",
    "FB_GAIN_CEIL = float(max(0.0, min(FB_GAIN_MAX, _a_dac, _a_adc)))\n",
    "#  Keep the probe clear of the boundary. FB_GAIN_CEIL can sit at K = 1 exactly\n",
    "#  (the closed-loop headroom formula stops there), and probing ON the boundary\n",
    "#  makes half the phases oscillate, leaves the cosine fit with too few points,\n",
    "#  and hands Step 8b a NaN phase.\n",
    "FB_PROBE_USE = float(min(FB_GAIN_PROBE, FB_GAIN_CEIL, 0.6 / max(G_FWD_RES, 1e-9)))\n",
    "FB_GAINS_USE = [round(fr * FB_GAIN_CEIL, 4) for fr in FB_GAIN_FRACS]\n",
    "\n",
    "print('  gain ceiling: %.2f from converter headroom, %.2f from the input guard'\n",
    "      % (_a_dac, _a_adc))\n",
    "if FB_GAIN_CEIL < 0.5 * FB_GAIN_MAX:\n",
    "    _d_ok = 0.9 * (_H - 0.0) / (1.0 + FB_GAIN_MAX * _r / max(1.0 - FB_GAIN_MAX * G_FWD_RES, 0.05))\n",
    "    print('  *** THE DRIVE IS EATING THE FEEDBACK RANGE: at DRIVE_FRAC = %.2f'\n",
    "          % DRIVE_FRAC)\n",
    "    print('  only A = %.2f fits (K = %.3f). Lower it to about %.2f and re-run.'\n",
    "          % (FB_GAIN_CEIL, FB_GAIN_CEIL * G_FWD_RES, max(0.05, min(0.3, _d_ok))))\n",
    "\n",
    "#  G_FWD_RES, not G_FWD: feedback acts only on the part of the returning signal\n",
    "#  that came out of the resonator. The off-resonance floor is fed back too, but\n",
    "#  it never touches the coil, so counting it over-predicts the loop gain.\n",
    "K_MAX_POSSIBLE = FB_GAIN_CEIL * G_FWD_RES\n",
    "K_AT_PROBE = FB_PROBE_USE * G_FWD_RES\n",
    "print('loop-gain budget')\n",
    "print('  one-way transfer, all of it    : %.5f  (%.1f dB)'\n",
    "      % (G_FWD, 20 * np.log10(max(G_FWD, 1e-12))))\n",
    "print('  ...of which went via the coil  : %.5f  (%.1f dB)   <- what feedback acts on'\n",
    "      % (G_FWD_RES, 20 * np.log10(max(G_FWD_RES, 1e-12))))\n",
    "print('  ...the rest is the floor       : %.0f%% of the returning amplitude'\n",
    "      % (100 * (1.0 - G_FWD_RES / max(G_FWD, 1e-12))))\n",
    "print('  converter headroom for feedback: %.3f of full scale' % _HEADROOM)\n",
    "print('  largest gain that fits in it   : %.2f' % FB_GAIN_CEIL)\n",
    "print('  gain ceiling actually used     : %.2f%s'\n",
    "      % (FB_GAIN_CEIL,\n",
    "         '  (capped by headroom, not by FB_GAIN_MAX = %.2f)' % FB_GAIN_MAX\n",
    "         if FB_GAIN_CEIL < FB_GAIN_MAX else '  (the register ceiling)'))\n",
    "print('  round trip at that ceiling     : K = %.4f' % K_MAX_POSSIBLE)\n",
    "print('  Q change that would produce    : %+.1f%%'\n",
    "      % (100 * (1.0 / (1.0 - min(K_MAX_POSSIBLE, 0.99)) - 1.0)))\n",
    "print('  K at the probe gain %.2f       : %.4f  (Q %+.1f%%)'\n",
    "      % (FB_PROBE_USE, K_AT_PROBE,\n",
    "         100 * (1.0 / (1.0 - min(K_AT_PROBE, 0.99)) - 1.0)))\n",
    "print('  drive + feedback at the DAC    : %.3f of full scale'\n",
    "      % (DRIVE_FRAC + FB_GAIN_CEIL * raw_peak))\n",
    "\n",
    "if K_MAX_POSSIBLE < 0.01:\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  *** THIS SWEEP CANNOT SHOW A FEEDBACK EFFECT. ***')\n",
    "    print('  Even at the register ceiling the loop gain is %.4f, which moves Q by'\n",
    "          % K_MAX_POSSIBLE)\n",
    "    print('  %.1f%% - below what a Lorentzian fit resolves. The sweep will run and'\n",
    "          % (100 * K_MAX_POSSIBLE))\n",
    "    print('  return flat Q against phase. That IS the measurement: with both ports')\n",
    "    print('  coupled through %.1f pF there is not enough gain in the loop to move a'\n",
    "          % (C_COUPLE * 1e12))\n",
    "    print('  real coil, and an amplifier in the pickup path is what changes it.')\n",
    "elif K_MAX_POSSIBLE < 0.05:\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  Marginal but workable: %.1f%% of Q at the ceiling. The differential'\n",
    "          % (100 * K_MAX_POSSIBLE))\n",
    "    print('  analysis below is what makes an effect this small readable.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  Comfortable: %.1f%% of Q at the ceiling.' % (100 * K_MAX_POSSIBLE))\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "print('probing %d phases at gain %.2f, %d averages per point'\n",
    "      % (len(FB_PHASES), FB_PROBE_USE, FB_NAVG))\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# +-4 linewidths, and wider than it looks it needs to be. Feedback both narrows\n",
    "# the line and shifts it, and a grid that the shifted line has walked out of\n",
    "# fails to fit at exactly the phases that matter most.\n",
    "grid8 = F0 + np.linspace(-4.0, 4.0, 33) * LW\n",
    "\n",
    "fb_phi, fb_q, fb_df = [], [], []\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    for phi in FB_PHASES:\n",
    "        ps.set(FB_PROBE_USE, phi)\n",
    "        time.sleep(SETTLE)\n",
    "        gen.freq(F0); gen.amp(DRIVE_FRAC); gen.run(); time.sleep(0.02)\n",
    "        lvl = sc.peak_frac(GUARD_NSAMP)\n",
    "        gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "        if lvl > FB_LEVEL_GUARD:\n",
    "            print('  %4d deg : ABANDONED, input at %.2f of full scale' % (phi, lvl))\n",
    "            fb_phi.append(phi); fb_q.append(np.nan); fb_df.append(np.nan)\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            f8, z8 = sweep(grid8, drive_frac=DRIVE_FRAC, navg=FB_NAVG,\n",
    "                           level_guard=FB_LEVEL_GUARD)\n",
    "            gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "            fit8 = fit_lorentzian(f8, np.abs(z8) ** 2)\n",
    "            # A saturated or oscillating loop still returns a \"fit\", and it can\n",
    "            # be absurd. Anything this far from the unfed line is not a\n",
    "            # measurement of the coil.\n",
    "            if not (0.02 * LW < fit8['lw'] < 50.0 * LW):\n",
    "                raise ValueError('width %.1f kHz is nowhere near the %.1f kHz '\n",
    "                                 'line - loop saturated?'\n",
    "                                 % (fit8['lw'] / 1e3, LW / 1e3))\n",
    "            fb_phi.append(phi); fb_q.append(fit8['Q']); fb_df.append(fit8['f0'] - F0)\n",
    "            print('  %4d deg : Q = %7.1f  (x%.2f),  centre %+8.1f Hz (%+.3f lw)'\n",
    "                  % (phi, fit8['Q'], fit8['Q'] / Q_SWEEP, fb_df[-1], fb_df[-1] / LW))\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:\n",
    "            fb_phi.append(phi); fb_q.append(np.nan); fb_df.append(np.nan)\n",
    "            print('  %4d deg : fit failed (%s)' % (phi, exc))\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    # The feedback loop is closed while this runs. Any exception, or\n",
    "    # a Ctrl-C between two phases, must not leave it that way.\n",
    "    ps.off()\n",
    "    gen.off()\n",
    "\n",
    "fb_phi = np.array(fb_phi, dtype=float)\n",
    "fb_q = np.array(fb_q, dtype=float)\n",
    "fb_df = np.array(fb_df, dtype=float)\n",
    "\n",
    "if np.all(~np.isfinite(fb_q)):\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError('every feedback point failed - check levels and coupling')\n",
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  DIFFERENTIAL ANALYSIS - phi against phi + 180\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  Feedback is antisymmetric in phase; drift, baseline bias and a sagging drive\n",
    "#  are not. Subtracting the opposite phase cancels those and doubles the signal.\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "half = len(fb_phi) // 2\n",
    "_opp = np.array([int(np.argmin(np.abs(((fb_phi - (p + 180.0)) + 180.0) % 360.0 - 180.0)))\n",
    "                 for p in fb_phi[:half]])\n",
    "dq = fb_q[:half] - fb_q[_opp]            # antisymmetric: the feedback signature\n",
    "ddf = fb_df[:half] - fb_df[_opp]\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- fit a cosine, do not take an argmax ------------------------------------\n",
    "#  Theory says the differential IS a cosine. An argmax returns a grid point,\n",
    "#  is biased to the ends of the half-turn, and discards eight of nine points.\n",
    "def _fit_cos(phi_deg, y):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Least-squares fit of y = D cos(phi - phi0). Returns (D, phi0_deg).\"\"\"\n",
    "    good = np.isfinite(y)\n",
    "    if int(np.count_nonzero(good)) < 3:\n",
    "        return float('nan'), float('nan')\n",
    "    p = np.radians(np.asarray(phi_deg, dtype=float)[good])\n",
    "    basis = np.column_stack([np.cos(p), np.sin(p)])\n",
    "    coef, _, _, _ = np.linalg.lstsq(basis, np.asarray(y, dtype=float)[good], rcond=-1)\n",
    "    return float(np.hypot(coef[0], coef[1])), float(np.degrees(np.arctan2(coef[1], coef[0])))\n",
    "\n",
    "_n_osc = int(np.sum(~np.isfinite(fb_q)))\n",
    "if _n_osc:\n",
    "    print('  %d of %d phases gave no fit (oscillating or level-guarded)'\n",
    "          % (_n_osc, len(fb_q)))\n",
    "DQ_AMP, PHI_NARROW = _fit_cos(fb_phi[:half], dq)\n",
    "DDF_AMP, PHI_SHIFT = _fit_cos(fb_phi[:half], ddf)\n",
    "PHI_NARROW = float(PHI_NARROW % 360.0)\n",
    "PHI_SHIFT = float(PHI_SHIFT % 360.0)\n",
    "PHI_BROAD = (PHI_NARROW + 180.0) % 360.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Noise from successive differences along a curve that should be smooth: the\n",
    "# measurement declaring its own error bar rather than us assuming one.\n",
    "_fin = fb_q[np.isfinite(fb_q)]\n",
    "Q_NOISE = float(np.std(np.diff(_fin)) / np.sqrt(2.0)) if len(_fin) > 2 else float('nan')\n",
    "FB_DETECTED = bool(np.isfinite(Q_NOISE) and DQ_AMP > 3.0 * Q_NOISE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Q+ = Q0/(1-K) and Q- = Q0/(1+K), so the differential amplitude is\n",
    "#     m = DQ_AMP / (2 Q0) = K / (1 - K^2)\n",
    "# which is K only for small K - it over-reads by 25% at K = 0.5 and diverges at\n",
    "# K = 1. Invert it exactly instead: K = (-1 + sqrt(1 + 4 m^2)) / (2 m).\n",
    "#  (Q+ - Q-)/(Q+ + Q-) = K exactly, for every pair, with Q0 cancelled. The\n",
    "#  cosine amplitude is only used to locate the phase: at large K the curve is\n",
    "#  Q0/(1 - K cos phi), which is peaked rather than sinusoidal, so its amplitude\n",
    "#  is not a good measure of K even though its symmetry still fixes the phase.\n",
    "_sq = fb_q[:half] + fb_q[_opp]\n",
    "with np.errstate(invalid='ignore', divide='ignore'):\n",
    "    _kp = dq / _sq\n",
    "K_MEASURED = float(np.nanmax(_kp)) if np.any(np.isfinite(_kp)) else 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "print('  differential amplitude       : %.2f%% of Q0' % (100 * DQ_AMP / Q_SWEEP))\n",
    "print('  MEASURED K                   : %.4f' % K_MEASURED)\n",
    "print('  predicted K, resonant only   : %.4f' % K_AT_PROBE)\n",
    "print('  (counting the floor as signal would predict %.4f)'\n",
    "      % (FB_PROBE_USE * G_FWD))\n",
    "print('  point-to-point Q noise       : %.2f%% of Q0' % (100 * Q_NOISE / Q_SWEEP))\n",
    "print('  signal-to-noise              : %.1f' % (DQ_AMP / max(Q_NOISE, 1e-12)))\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "if not FB_DETECTED:\n",
    "    print('  NO FEEDBACK EFFECT DETECTED - and the phases below are meaningless.')\n",
    "    print('  The modulation is under three times the noise, so the \"narrowing')\n",
    "    print('  phase\" is just wherever the noise peaked. Do NOT read it as physics,')\n",
    "    print('  and do not read Step 8b\\'s K either.')\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    if K_MAX_POSSIBLE < 0.01:\n",
    "        print('  This agrees with the budget above: the loop simply has no gain.')\n",
    "        print('  The fix is not in this notebook. Either put a low-noise amplifier')\n",
    "        print('  in the pickup path before IN1, or couple more strongly than')\n",
    "        print('  %.1f pF - both of which change the divider, and with it every' % (C_COUPLE * 1e12))\n",
    "        print('  number Step 4 predicted.')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('  The budget said an effect SHOULD be visible, so this disagreement')\n",
    "        print('  is worth chasing: check the delay line configured above, check')\n",
    "        print('  that the phase shifter is not bypassed, and re-run Step 4 to')\n",
    "        print('  confirm the coupling has not changed.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('  narrowing phase (cosine fit)   : %.1f deg' % PHI_NARROW)\n",
    "    print('  broadening phase (opposite)    : %.1f deg' % PHI_BROAD)\n",
    "    print('  largest centre shift at        : %.1f deg' % PHI_SHIFT)\n",
    "    _sep = (PHI_SHIFT - PHI_NARROW) % 360.0\n",
    "    print('  separation between them        : %.1f deg  (theory: 90 or 270)' % _sep)\n",
    "    _off = min(abs(_sep - 90.0), abs(_sep - 270.0))\n",
    "    if _off > 35.0:\n",
    "        print('  WARNING: the two effects should be a quarter turn apart and are')\n",
    "        print('  %.0f degrees off it. At a signal-to-noise of %.1f that is unlikely'\n",
    "              % (_off, DQ_AMP / max(Q_NOISE, 1e-12)))\n",
    "        print('  to be scatter - suspect the loop compressing, or a second path')\n",
    "        print('  with its own phase (see the leakage figure in Step 4).')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('  -> a quarter turn, as theory demands. The phase axis is sound.')\n",
    "\n",
    "    _ratio = K_MEASURED / max(FB_PROBE_USE * G_FWD_RES, 1e-12)\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  measured K / predicted K : %.2fx' % _ratio)\n",
    "    print('  round-trip transfer from the loop : %.5f  (%.1f dB)'\n",
    "          % (K_MEASURED / FB_PROBE_USE,\n",
    "             20 * np.log10(max(K_MEASURED / FB_PROBE_USE, 1e-12))))\n",
    "    print('  The measured value is the measurement; the budget rests on estimated')\n",
    "    print('  capacitances, so a factor of two either way means little.')\n",
    "    if not (0.33 < _ratio < 3.0):\n",
    "        print('  -> over 3x apart: compare the transfer above with Step 4b.')"
   ]
  },
