   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# Step 8d — The lineshape family\n",
    "\n",
    "Herkenhoff's Fig. 6.3 shows the resonator's **noise** spectrum at a series of feedback gains,\n",
    "positive and negative: the line sharpens and rises with positive feedback, flattens with\n",
    "negative.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The noise version is not obtainable here.** Step 4 measures the coil's Johnson noise arriving\n",
    "at 0.21 nV/√Hz against a converter floor of 4.46 — twenty times under. Herkenhoff's resonator is\n",
    "cryogenic with a low-noise amplifier at the tank, which is what makes the bell shape visible at\n",
    "all without driving it.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The driven equivalent is**, and it carries the same information: sweep the drive across the\n",
    "line at each feedback setting and plot the response in decibels. Same family of curves, obtained\n",
    "by driving rather than by listening.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Both signs are available.** The coefficient register holds an amplitude in [0, 1.99) and cannot\n",
    "go negative, but negative feedback is simply the opposite phase — `A` at `φ_narrow + 180°`. That\n",
    "is exactly what the thesis's negative `G̃` curves are.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 8d - LINESHAPE AT A FAMILY OF FEEDBACK GAINS  (thesis Fig. 6.3)\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 8d - lineshape versus feedback gain, both signs')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "FB_8D_OK = bool(FB_8B_OK)\n",
    "if not FB_8D_OK:\n",
    "    print('SKIPPED - Step 8a found no usable narrowing phase, so there is no')\n",
    "    print('meaningful axis to sweep along. Not a fault in this step.')\n",
    "\n",
    "if FB_8D_OK:\n",
    "    acq.start(DEC_USE)\n",
    "    ps.config_delay(F0)\n",
    "    grid8d = F0 + np.linspace(-5.0, 5.0, 61) * LW\n",
    "    spec_f, spec_p, spec_lbl, spec_K = [], [], [], []\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        for fr in FB_SPEC_FRACS:\n",
    "            A = abs(fr) * FB_GAIN_CEIL\n",
    "            phi = PHI_NARROW if fr >= 0 else PHI_BROAD\n",
    "            ps.set(A, phi)\n",
    "            time.sleep(SETTLE)\n",
    "            gen.amp(0.0); time.sleep(0.005)\n",
    "            if sc.peak_frac(GUARD_NSAMP) > FB_OSC_LEVEL:\n",
    "                ps.off(); print('  %+.2f : oscillating, skipped' % fr); continue\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                fs_, zs_ = sweep(grid8d, drive_frac=DRIVE_FRAC, navg=FB_NAVG,\n",
    "                                 level_guard=FB_LEVEL_GUARD)\n",
    "                fit = fit_lorentzian(fs_, np.abs(zs_) ** 2)\n",
    "                spec_f.append(fs_); spec_p.append(np.abs(zs_) ** 2)\n",
    "                spec_lbl.append(fr); spec_K.append(1.0 - Q_SWEEP / fit['Q'])\n",
    "                print('  %+.2f of ceiling (A = %.2f, %s) : Q = %7.1f (x%.2f), K = %+.3f'\n",
    "                      % (fr, A, 'narrowing' if fr >= 0 else 'broadening',\n",
    "                         fit['Q'], fit['Q'] / Q_SWEEP, spec_K[-1]))\n",
    "            except Exception as exc:\n",
    "                print('  %+.2f : %s' % (fr, exc))\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        ps.off(); gen.off()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if len(spec_p) < 2:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError('too few usable spectra')\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  Q spans %.0f to %.0f  (no feedback %.0f)'\n",
    "          % (min(Q_SWEEP / (1 - k) for k in spec_K), max(Q_SWEEP / (1 - k) for k in spec_K),\n",
    "             Q_SWEEP))\n"
   ],
