   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# Step 8e — How far, and how accurately, the resonance can be moved\n",
    "\n",
    "Thesis Fig. 6.2 shows the resonance pushed 2.78 kHz aside by feedback, decoupling the ion from\n",
    "the detection system. Two questions follow, and this step answers both by measurement:\n",
    "\n",
    "**How far?** Feedback in quadrature with the coil's motion shifts the centre rather than the\n",
    "damping, so the sweep runs at `φ_shift` — a quarter turn from the narrowing phase — and at the\n",
    "opposite phase for the other direction. Expressed in **linewidths**, which is the number that\n",
    "matters for decoupling and the only fair comparison against a resonator of different Q.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How accurately?** The shift-versus-gain curve is fitted, inverted to request a set of target\n",
    "shifts, and each one applied and re-measured. The residual is the accuracy with which a wanted\n",
    "detuning can actually be set.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 8e - FREQUENCY SHIFT: RANGE AND ACCURACY\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 8e - how far and how accurately the resonance moves')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "FB_8E_OK = bool(FB_8B_OK)\n",
    "if not FB_8E_OK:\n",
    "    print('SKIPPED - Step 8a found no usable narrowing phase, so there is no')\n",
    "    print('meaningful axis to sweep along. Not a fault in this step.')\n",
    "\n",
    "if FB_8E_OK:\n",
    "    acq.start(DEC_USE)\n",
    "    ps.config_delay(F0)\n",
    "    PHI_SHIFT_OPP = (PHI_SHIFT + 180.0) % 360.0\n",
    "    sh_gain, sh_df = [], []\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _shift_at(A, phi):\n",
    "        \"\"\"Centre shift with the loop closed at (A, phi). Returns Hz, or None.\"\"\"\n",
    "        ps.set(A, phi)\n",
    "        time.sleep(SETTLE)\n",
    "        gen.amp(0.0); time.sleep(0.005)\n",
    "        if sc.peak_frac(GUARD_NSAMP) > FB_OSC_LEVEL:\n",
    "            ps.off(); return None\n",
    "        fq, zq = sweep(F0 + np.linspace(-4.0, 4.0, 33) * LW, drive_frac=DRIVE_FRAC,\n",
    "                       navg=FB_NAVG, level_guard=FB_LEVEL_GUARD)\n",
    "        ft = fit_lorentzian(fq, np.abs(zq) ** 2)\n",
    "        if not (0.02 * LW < ft['lw'] < 50.0 * LW):\n",
    "            return None\n",
    "        return ft['f0'] - F0\n",
    "\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        for phi, sgn in ((PHI_SHIFT, +1), (PHI_SHIFT_OPP, -1)):\n",
    "            for fr in FB_SHIFT_FRACS:\n",
    "                A = fr * FB_GAIN_CEIL\n",
    "                try:\n",
    "                    d = _shift_at(A, phi)\n",
    "                except Exception:\n",
    "                    d = None\n",
    "                if d is None:\n",
    "                    continue\n",
    "                sh_gain.append(sgn * A); sh_df.append(d)\n",
    "                print('  A = %5.2f at %5.1f deg : shift %+9.1f Hz (%+.3f linewidths)'\n",
    "                      % (A, phi, d, d / LW))\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        ps.off(); gen.off()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if len(sh_df) < 4:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError('too few usable shift points')\n",
    "    sh_gain = np.array(sh_gain); sh_df = np.array(sh_df)\n",
    "    SHIFT_MAX = float(np.max(np.abs(sh_df)))\n",
    "    _ord = np.argsort(sh_gain)\n",
    "    _slope = float(np.polyfit(sh_gain, sh_df, 1)[0])\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  RANGE   : %+.1f to %+.1f Hz  =  %+.2f to %+.2f linewidths'\n",
    "          % (sh_df.min(), sh_df.max(), sh_df.min() / LW, sh_df.max() / LW))\n",
    "    print('            %.3f%% of the centre frequency' % (100 * SHIFT_MAX / F0))\n",
    "    print('  slope   : %.0f Hz per unit gain' % _slope)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ---- accuracy: request a shift, apply it, measure what you got --------------\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  ACCURACY - requesting a shift and measuring the result')\n",
    "    _targets = np.linspace(0.35, 0.85, FB_SHIFT_TESTS) * SHIFT_MAX\n",
    "    _err = []\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        for tgt in _targets:\n",
    "            A_req = float(np.clip(abs(tgt / _slope), 0.0, FB_GAIN_CEIL))\n",
    "            got = _shift_at(A_req, PHI_SHIFT if _slope > 0 else PHI_SHIFT_OPP)\n",
    "            if got is None:\n",
    "                print('    target %+8.1f Hz : abandoned' % tgt); continue\n",
    "            _err.append(got - tgt)\n",
    "            print('    target %+8.1f Hz -> A = %.2f -> got %+8.1f Hz  (error %+7.1f Hz'\n",
    "                  ', %+.3f lw)' % (tgt, A_req, got, got - tgt, (got - tgt) / LW))\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        ps.off(); gen.off()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if _err:\n",
    "        SHIFT_RMS_ERR = float(np.sqrt(np.mean(np.square(_err))))\n",
    "        print('')\n",
    "        print('  rms error : %.1f Hz = %.4f linewidths = %.1f ppm of f0'\n",
    "              % (SHIFT_RMS_ERR, SHIFT_RMS_ERR / LW, 1e6 * SHIFT_RMS_ERR / F0))\n",
    "        _drift = globals().get('DRIFT_HZ_PER_MIN', float('nan'))\n",
    "        if np.isfinite(_drift):\n",
    "            print('  Step 7 measured the coil drifting %.1f Hz/min unaided, so a shift'\n",
    "                  % abs(_drift))\n",
    "            print('  can be set %s accurately as the coil holds still.'\n",
    "                  % ('more' if SHIFT_RMS_ERR < abs(_drift) else 'less'))\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        SHIFT_RMS_ERR = float('nan')\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# --- Step 8e picture --------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "if globals().get('sh_df') is None or len(sh_df) < 2:\n",
    "    print('Step 8d/8e produced no data - nothing to plot.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    fig, (a1, a2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(9.6, 4.0))\n",
    "    a1.plot(sh_gain[_ord], sh_df[_ord] / 1e3, 'o-', color=CLR_BLUE)\n",
    "    a1.plot(sh_gain[_ord], _slope * sh_gain[_ord] / 1e3, '--', color=CLR_GREY,\n",
    "            label='%.0f Hz per unit gain' % _slope)\n",
    "    a1.axhline(0.0, ls=':', color=CLR_GREY)\n",
    "    a1.set_xlabel('signed feedback gain (negative = opposite phase)')\n",
    "    a1.set_ylabel('centre shift / kHz')\n",
    "    a1.set_title('(a)  range')\n",
    "    a1.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "    _lwax = sh_df[_ord] / LW\n",
    "    a2.plot(sh_gain[_ord], _lwax, 'o-', color=CLR_ORANGE)\n",
    "    a2.axhline(0.0, ls=':', color=CLR_GREY)\n",
    "    a2.set_xlabel('signed feedback gain')\n",
    "    a2.set_ylabel('centre shift / linewidths')\n",
    "    a2.set_title('(b)  in linewidths - the portable number')\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "    print('Panel (b) is the fair comparison against a resonator of any Q: a shift of')\n",
    "    print('one linewidth decouples as effectively at 40 MHz as at 740 kHz.')\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 9 — Close the loop on the instrument, and write down what was learned\n",
    "\n",
    "Two things happen here, in this order.\n",
    "\n",
    "**First, the self-test is run again.** If it passed at the start and passes now, nothing about\n",
    "the instrument changed while you were measuring the coil — so the numbers below are about the\n",
    "coil. If it passed then and fails now, the coil measurements are not trustworthy and the\n",
    "reason is in the board, not the physics. This is the one check that no amount of care with the\n",
    "coil can substitute for, and it costs ten seconds.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Then everything measured is written to a file**, so the next notebook does not have to be\n",
    "told the answer by hand. That was the one thing the emulator made free and a real coil does\n",
    "not: `reso.config()` used to be read back in about forty places. Now there is a file instead."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 9a - THE SELF-TEST, AGAIN\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 9 - closing checks')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('re-running the instrument self-test...')\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "st1_after = instrument_selftest()\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "if st1_before['ok'] and st1_after['ok']:\n",
    "    print('The instrument returned a known answer BEFORE and AFTER the session.')\n",
    "    print('Nothing about the board changed while the coil was being measured.')\n",
    "elif st1_before['ok'] and not st1_after['ok']:\n",
    "    print('*** The self-test passed at the start and FAILS now. ***')\n",
    "    print('Something changed during the session - a reload, a thermal problem, a')\n",
    "    print('register left in an odd state. Treat every coil number below as')\n",
    "    print('provisional until this passes again.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('*** The self-test was already failing. Nothing below is trustworthy. ***')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 9b - SUMMARY\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "def _g(name, default=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Fetch a result that an earlier step may have skipped.\"\"\"\n",
    "    v = globals().get(name, default)\n",
    "    return default if v is None else v\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "_qa = globals().get('Q_ALT', None)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
